      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
</exercise>
 </page>
 <page>


<definition xml:id="def-expected-values-continuous">
  <statement>
    <p>
      The expected value, variance, and standard deviation are defined similarly for continuous random variables as
      they were for discrete:
    </p>

    <p>
      Let <m>X</m> a continuous random variable:
      <md>
        E[u(X)] = \int_{-\infty}^{\infty}u(x) \cdot f(x) \, dx
      </md>
      <md>
        \mu = E[X] = \int_{-\infty}^{\infty}x \cdot f(x) \, dx
      </md>
      <md>
        Var(X) = \sigma^{2} = E[(X-\mu)^{2}] = \int_{-\infty}^{\infty}(x-\mu)^{2} \cdot f(x) \, dx
      </md>
      <md>
        \sigma = \sqrt{Var(X)}
      </md>
    </p>

    <p>
      The Moment Generating Function:
      <md>
        M(t) = E[e^{tX}] = \int_{-\infty}^{\infty}e^{tx}\cdot f(x) \, dx\,\,\, -h \leq t \leq h
      </md>
      provided the integral exists for some <m>h</m> (interval around 0). As with the discrete case we have the following relationships:
    </p>

    <p>
   
      <md>
        \sigma^{2} = E[X^{2}]-\mu^{2}
      </md>
      <md>
        M^{(n)}(0) = E[X^{n}]
      </md>
      <md>
        M'(0) = \mu
      </md>
      <md>
        \sigma^{2} = M''(0) - [M'(0)]^{2}
      </md>
    </p>
  </statement>
</definition>

<exercise workspace="2in">
  <statement>
    <p>
      Let <m>X</m> be a continuous R.V. with pdf
      <m>
        f(x)=3x^{2}, \,\, 0 \leq x \leq 1
      </m>
      Find <m>E[2x-1]</m>.
    </p>
  </statement>
  </exercise>
    </page>
    <page>

  
<exercise workspace="3in">
  <statement>
     <p>
      Let <m>X</m> be a continuous R.V. with pdf
      <m>f(x) = {\frac{1}{2\sqrt{x}}}, \,\, 0 \lt x \leq 1</m> Find
      <m>\mu</m> and <m>\sigma^2</m>.
    </p>
  </statement>
</exercise>
</page>
<page>
<exercise workspace="6in">
  <statement>
     <p>
      Let <m>X</m> be a continuous RV on <m>0 \leq x \leq \infty</m> with pdf
      <m>f(x)=xe^{-x}</m>. Check that <m>\int_{0}^{\infty}f(x)\, dx = 1</m>.
      
    </p>
  </statement>
</exercise>
</page>
<page>
<exercise workspace = "6in">
  <statement>
    <p>
      Let <m>X \sim U(a,b)</m> be a continuous uniform R.V. on <m>[a,b]</m>.
      Find <m>\mu, \sigma^{2},</m> and <m>M(t)</m>.
    </p>
  </statement>
</exercise>
</page>
<page>

  <exercise>
    <introduction>
      <p>
         Let <m>X</m> be a continuous RV with pdf given by
            <m>f(x)=cx^{2}, \,\, -1\lt x\lt 1</m>.
      </p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace = "2in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          What value must <m>c</m> be to make this a valid pdf?
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find <m>P(X \leq 0)</m>
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>
           Find <m>\mu</m>
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find <m>\sigma^{2}</m>.
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>
 </page>
 <page>
<exercise>
  <introduction>
    <p>
       Let <m>X\sim U(1,6)</m>.
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <task workspace = "0.5in">
    <statement>
      <p>
         What is the pdf of <m>X, f(x)</m>?
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
  <task workspace = "1.5in">
    <statement>
      <p>
      Find <m>\mu</m> and <m>\sigma^2</m> (you may use the formulas for the uniform distribution).
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
  <task workspace = ".75in">
    <statement>
      <p>
         What is the cdf of <m>X, F(x)</m>?
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
  <task workspace=".75in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        Use the cdf to find <m>P(2.5 \leq X \leq 4)</m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
</exercise>    
</page>
<page>
<exercise>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      Let <m>X</m> be a continuous RV with pdf
            <m>f(x)=4x, \,\, 0 \lt x\lt c</m>.
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <task workspace="1in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        What value of <m>c</m> makes this a valid pdf?
